  "content": {
    "id": "p35-q27-30",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve the following for $0^\\circ\\le\\theta\\le360^\\circ$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p35-q27",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=\\sin70^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=20^\\circ,\\ 340^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\cos(90^\\circ-70^\\circ)\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\cos20^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nCosine is positive in quadrants I and IV; the related angle is $20^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=20^\\circ,\\ 360^\\circ-20^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=20^\\circ,\\ 340^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q28",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\theta=\\cot160^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=110^\\circ,\\ 290^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\tan(90^\\circ-160^\\circ)\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\tan(-70^\\circ)\\\\\\tan\\theta&=-\\tan70^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nTangent is negative in quadrants II and IV; the related angle is $70^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-70^\\circ,\\ 360^\\circ-70^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=110^\\circ,\\ 290^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q29",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=\\cos205^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=245^\\circ,\\ 295^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta&=\\cos(180^\\circ+25^\\circ)\\\\\\sin\\theta&=-\\cos25^\\circ\\\\\\sin\\theta&=-\\sin65^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nSine is negative in quadrants III and IV; the related angle is $65^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ+65^\\circ,\\ 360^\\circ-65^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=245^\\circ,\\ 295^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q30",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=\\sin310^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=140^\\circ,\\ 220^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\sin(360^\\circ-50^\\circ)\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\sin50^\\circ\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\cos40^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nCosine is negative in quadrants II and III; the related angle is $40^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-40^\\circ,\\ 180^\\circ+40^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=140^\\circ,\\ 220^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
